title: The Envoy Gives Orders
subtitle: Moscow's man in Berlin goes over the Zentrale's head.
new-page: true
tags: event
priority: -1
view-if: {!
if (typeof RG === 'undefined') { return false; }
if (!RG.lw && this.game.scenes.lw_lib) { this._runActions(this.game.scenes.lw_lib.onArrival); }
return !!(RG.lw && RG.lw.ready('m_envoy'));
!}
on-arrival: {!
if (!RG.lw) { this._runActions(this.game.scenes.lw_lib.onArrival); }
RG.lw.fire('m_envoy');
RG.lw.setD(RG.lw.best(function (d) { return !RG.lw.ours(d); }, function (d) { return -RG.lw.dv(d, 'loyalty'); }) || RG.lw.best(function () { return true; }, function (d) { return RG.lw.dv(d, 'militancy'); }));
Q.lw_name = Q.comintern_rep;
!}

= The Envoy Gives Orders

**[+ lw_name +]**, the Executive's representative in Berlin, has written directly to the district leadership of [+ lw_d_name +], without telling the Zentrale. His letter is signed in the name of the Executive. [? if lw_d_fcode = 2 or lw_d_fcode = 4 : It instructs the district to prepare its members "for the coming battles". ?][? if lw_d_fcode = 1 or lw_d_fcode = 3 : It instructs the district to stop its "opportunist hesitation" and fall in line with the International. ?]

The district secretary has sent a copy to Berlin, and asks who leads the German party.

- @accept: Accept the envoy's authority.
- @protest: Complain to [+ ecci_friend_name +] on the Executive.
- @bar: Bar him from all party business.

@accept
subtitle: [? if lock_moscow_orders = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] Moscow's man has the last word. The whole Executive is pleased.
choose-if: lock_moscow_orders < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids taking orders from Moscow.
on-arrival: {!
RG.lw.against('moscow_orders');
Q.independence -= 6;
RG.ecci('all', 5);
RG.district(Q.lw_d, {loyalty: -6});
!}

The Zentrale confirms the envoy's instructions. The district secretaries now know there are two addresses in Berlin.

@protest
subtitle: [? if ecci_friend_favour >= 55 : Our friend there may well get him recalled. ?][? if ecci_friend_favour < 55 : Our friend there has little weight to spend. ?] If not, the envoy stays, and knows who complained.
on-arrival: {!
RG.ecci(Q.ecci_friend, -3);
Q.independence += 3;
if (Q.ecci_friend_favour >= 55 && Math.random() < 0.55) {
    Q.lw_out = 1;
    RG.news('The Executive recalls ' + Q.comintern_rep + ' from Berlin', 2);
    Q.comintern_rep = 0;
    RG.ecci('zinoviev', -4);
} else {
    Q.lw_out = 2;
    RG.ecci('zinoviev', -3);
}
!}

[? if lw_out = 1 : [+ ecci_friend_name +] raises the matter at the Executive. A month later, [+ lw_name +] is called back to Moscow "for consultations", and does not return. ?][? if lw_out = 2 : The answer from Moscow regrets the misunderstanding and confirms the envoy in his post. He knows who complained. ?]

@bar
subtitle: The Zentrale is master in its own house. Every man on the Executive takes it as an insult.
on-arrival: {!
Q.independence += 8;
RG.ecci('all', -6);
RG.lw.lean('luxemburgist', 1, 4);
RG.news('German Zentrale breaks with the Executive\'s envoy', 2);
!}

[+ lw_name +] is told that he is welcome in Germany as a guest, and that he will no longer receive the Zentrale's minutes or its district addresses.
